---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "April 26, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How the Cosmo site handles your data: cookieless analytics, no tracking, no third-party advertising."
  noindex={true}
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-24 pt-32 sm:py-32">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-secondary dark:text-brand-tertiary">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-tertiary shadow-[0_0_10px_currentColor]"></span>
        <span>Legal</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-5 font-heading text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-brand-secondary dark:text-brand-tertiary">
        Last updated {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-cosmo space-y-10 text-brand-primary/90 dark:text-brand-quaternary/90">
      <section>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
          This site (<code>cosmo.dyslecix.dev</code>) is the marketing and
          documentation home for the
          <a href="https://github.com/DyslecixDev/cosmo" class="underline decoration-brand-tertiary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand-tertiary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cosmo template</a>.
          It is operated by Christian Demesa as an individual ("we", "us").
          The site is static &mdash; no accounts, no forms, no comments, no
          advertising &mdash; and we collect as little as technically
          possible.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          We do not set any cookies. We use two <code>localStorage</code>
          entries — <code>theme</code> to remember your light or dark mode
          preference, and <code>motion</code> to remember whether you have
          paused animations. Both values are only ever read and written
          locally in your browser, never sent to a server, and not used to
          identify you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">Cloudflare</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          We use
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/" class="underline decoration-brand-tertiary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand-tertiary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare, Inc.</a>
          (United States) for hosting and content delivery (Cloudflare
          Pages), cookieless web analytics (Cloudflare Web Analytics), and
          cookieless real user monitoring of page performance (Cloudflare
          Observatory). As a result, Cloudflare processes on our behalf:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-relaxed">
          <li>Standard request metadata &mdash; IP address, user agent, and timestamp &mdash; to deliver content, cache responses, and protect the site against abuse.</li>
          <li>Aggregated, anonymized analytics such as page URL, referrer, approximate country, and browser/device type. No fingerprinting; no cross-site tracking.</li>
          <li>Anonymized performance metrics for the page you loaded &mdash; Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS), navigation timing (TTFB, FCP), connection type, and approximate country.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          We do not maintain our own server-side request logs, databases, or
          analytics stores. See Cloudflare's
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" class="underline decoration-brand-tertiary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand-tertiary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>
          for how it handles data as a processor.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">Third-party content on this site</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          The landing page embeds a small badge image from
          <a href="https://shields.io/" class="underline decoration-brand-tertiary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand-tertiary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">shields.io</a>
          that displays this project's GitHub star count. When the page
          loads, your browser fetches that image directly from
          <code>img.shields.io</code>, so shields.io may receive standard
          HTTP request metadata such as your IP address, user agent, and
          referring page. We do not receive that data ourselves.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">International data transfers</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          The site is served from Cloudflare's global network, and request
          data may be processed by Cloudflare in the United States and in
          other countries where Cloudflare operates. If you are visiting
          from the EU/EEA, the UK, or Switzerland, this transfer is
          conducted under the European Commission's Standard Contractual
          Clauses (SCCs) as part of Cloudflare's Data Processing Addendum.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">Legal basis for processing (EU/UK GDPR)</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Where the EU or UK GDPR applies, we rely on
          <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR) as
          the legal basis for the limited processing described above
          &mdash; specifically, our interest in delivering the site
          reliably, keeping it secure, and understanding aggregate usage and
          performance. Because we use no cookies or other identifiers that
          would require consent for these purposes, no consent banner is
          shown.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">Data retention</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          We do not retain any personal data ourselves. Data Cloudflare
          processes on our behalf is retained according to Cloudflare's own
          retention policies. If you contact us by email, that
          correspondence remains in our email inbox until we delete it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">Your rights (EU/UK GDPR)</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          If the EU or UK GDPR applies to you, you have the rights of
          access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data
          portability, and the right to object with respect to data
          processed on our behalf. You also have the right to lodge a
          complaint with your local supervisory authority (your national
          data protection authority in the EU, or the Information
          Commissioner's Office in the UK). To exercise any of these
          rights, contact us at the address below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">Email contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          If you contact us by email, your message and email address are
          processed by Google LLC as our email provider (Gmail). Google's
          handling of that data is governed by its own privacy policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-primary dark:text-brand-quaternary">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          For questions about this policy or to exercise any of the rights
          above, you can reach Christian Demesa at
          <a href="mailto:dyslecixdev@gmail.com" class="underline decoration-brand-tertiary/60 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-brand-tertiary">dyslecixdev@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
